poor daily save and fair those are the  key words in a proposal for a new  European Asylum system presented by the  EU Commission today let's be clear  migration will be one of the main  challenges the European Union has to  face together in the longer term this  issue is not going away so Europe will  need sustainable future proof migration  policies that provide orderly and safe  pathways to the EU the existing  so-called Dublin rules on migration have  been criticised there many as obsolete  and unfair to countries like Greece and  Italy the proposed reforms suggest two  options option one keeps the current  system in place but would give countries  under particular pressure the  possibility to call for help the  fairness mechanism would then allow them  to resettle migrants within the EU a  second more drastic option would scrap  the Dublin rules a European agency could  then in the long run distribute asylum  seekers according to a permanent quota  but members of the European Parliament  are already criticizing this approach  that is for entirely Cafaro PA  news and I'd find the creation of this  kind of institution at a European level  bizarre of course we need to think about  why the same categories of people are  more likely to be granted asylum in some  states than in others but the solution  cannot involve centralizing these tasks  we need better coordination boozy  peasant redundant upstream the proposed  reform presents fundamental change to  how the EU deals with asylum seekers but  including a permanent distribution  scheme for migrants has always been  fiercely opposed by Central and Eastern  European countries and there are no  signs that their position is going to  change anytime soon
 

